</section>

<section class="sec deep" id="answers"><div class="wrap">
  <nav class="topics" aria-label="Topics">
    <a href="#money">Money and cost</a><a href="#start">Getting started</a><a href="#privacy">Who sees what</a><a href="#records">Answering a record</a><a href="#groups">Groups</a><a href="#business">Businesses</a>
  </nav>
  <p class="count" id="faq-count" aria-live="polite"></p>
  <div class="faq">
<section class="topic" id="money" aria-labelledby="money-h"><h2 id="money-h">Money and cost</h2><details class="qa" open><summary><span>What does it cost?</span><svg class="chev" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-cd"/></svg></summary><div class="ans"><p>Sawaza is free to use: write records, send them and keep them, with no fees.</p></div></details><details class="qa"><summary><span>Does Sawaza touch my money?</span><svg class="chev" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-cd"/></svg></summary><div class="ans" data-new="1"><p>No. It records money. It never holds it or moves it. You pay the way you always do, in cash, by Mobile Money or through a bank, and Sawaza keeps the record of it.</p></div></details><details class="qa"><summary><span>Will Sawaza ever ask me to send money?</span><svg class="chev" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-cd"/></svg></summary><div class="ans" data-new="1"><p>No. Sawaza never asks you to send money. A message that asks you to pay in order to see or confirm a record did not come from Sawaza.</p></div></details></section>
<section class="topic" id="start" aria-labelledby="start-h"><h2 id="start-h">Getting started</h2><details class="qa"><summary><span>What is Sawaza?</span><svg class="chev" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-cd"/></svg></summary><div class="ans" data-new="1"><p>Sawaza keeps one record of money between two people, signed by both. You write what happened and say which way it went: paid or received, lent or borrowed, sold or bought on credit. The other side confirms it, and you both hold the same copy and read from the same page.</p></div></details><details class="qa"><summary><span>How do I sign in?</span><svg class="chev" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-cd"/></svg></summary><div class="ans" data-new="1"><p>With your phone number. Sawaza sends a six-digit code to that number, and your number is the one thing it verifies. There is no password and no email to remember.</p></div></details><details class="qa"><summary><span>I lost my phone. Are my records gone?</span><svg class="chev" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-cd"/></svg></summary><div class="ans" data-new="1"><p>No. Sign in with the same number on a new phone and your records are there.</p></div></details><details class="qa"><summary><span>Do I need a signal to write a record?</span><svg class="chev" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-cd"/></svg></summary><div class="ans" data-new="1"><p>No. Sawaza works without network. What you write is kept on your phone and sent when you are back online.</p></div></details><details class="qa"><summary><span>The other person is not on Sawaza. Can I still write a record?</span><svg class="chev" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-cd"/></svg></summary><div class="ans" data-new="1"><p>Yes. Pick a phone contact, type a number, or write a name alone. Someone on Sawaza is asked to confirm it in the app. A number not on Sawaza yet gets a link on WhatsApp or SMS, and the record waits for them. A name alone stays with you. Nothing is signed from the notification: they open the record and answer it there. Don't wait for their book. Start yours.</p></div></details><details class="qa"><summary><span>What can I keep for myself?</span><svg class="chev" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-cd"/></svg></summary><div class="ans" data-new="1"><p>Your records and who owes what, your cash, bank and mobile money accounts, and things you own, such as land or a motorbike, with what they cost. Spaces are like folders for your records: keep a plot, a farm or a shop apart from your own money. Each record lands in the space you pick, and how you file it never changes it for the other side.</p></div></details></section>
<section class="topic" id="privacy" aria-labelledby="privacy-h"><h2 id="privacy-h">Who sees what</h2><details class="qa"><summary><span>Who sees my records?</span><svg class="chev" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-cd"/></svg></summary><div class="ans"><p>Only the people you choose to share them with. You can write a record about someone and keep it to yourself: it stays private until you send it, and you never have to.</p></div></details><details class="qa"><summary><span>Does Sawaza read my phonebook?</span><svg class="chev" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-cd"/></svg></summary><div class="ans" data-new="1"><p>The names in your phonebook stay on your phone. Only you see who you add and what you call them.</p></div></details><details class="qa"><summary><span>Can I delete a record?</span><svg class="chev" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-cd"/></svg></summary><div class="ans" data-new="1"><p>You can remove your own copy, never the other side's. Their copy stays theirs.</p></div></details><details class="qa"><summary><span>What is shared on a record, and what is only mine?</span><svg class="chev" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-cd"/></svg></summary><div class="ans" data-new="1"><p>Shared: the amount, who paid whom, the day, both signatures and every answer to it. Yours alone: the item, the space and the account you file it under, and the name you saved the person as. If you saved him as David Landlord, the record still says David.</p></div></details><details class="qa"><summary><span>Who can see a photo or receipt I attach?</span><svg class="chev" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-cd"/></svg></summary><div class="ans" data-new="1"><p>Only the people who can read its record.</p></div></details><details class="qa"><summary><span>How do I know a number or a name is real?</span><svg class="chev" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-cd"/></svg></summary><div class="ans" data-new="1"><p>A number shows On Sawaza once it is proved. A name shows who gave it: Self-declared, or Named by the writer.</p></div></details><details class="qa"><summary><span>How do I delete my account?</span><svg class="chev" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-cd"/></svg></summary><div class="ans" data-new="1"><p>Delete your account from Settings. A record someone else signed with you stays in their copy.</p></div></details></section>
<section class="topic" id="records" aria-labelledby="records-h"><h2 id="records-h">Answering a record</h2><details class="qa"><summary><span>Someone sent me a record. What can I do?</span><svg class="chev" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-cd"/></svg></summary><div class="ans" data-new="1"><p>Open it and choose one answer:</p><ul><li><b>Confirm, I received it</b>, when it happened as written.</li><li><b>The details are wrong</b>: say what the figure should be, and they are asked to confirm it.</li><li><b>This isn't mine</b>: decline it, and it stays off your books.</li></ul><p>You can also tap Later and come back to it. Nothing signs from a notification: only your answer on the record does.</p></div></details><details class="qa"><summary><span>What does confirming mean?</span><svg class="chev" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-cd"/></svg></summary><div class="ans" data-new="1"><p>Confirming says the record happened as written. It is not a judgement on the price.</p></div></details><details class="qa"><summary><span>What does Awaiting mean?</span><svg class="chev" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-cd"/></svg></summary><div class="ans" data-new="1"><p>A record is sealed only when everyone it names has signed. Until then it says where it stands on both phones: Waiting on the person who has not signed, Contested, or Declined.</p></div></details><details class="qa"><summary><span>What if the details are wrong?</span><svg class="chev" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-cd"/></svg></summary><div class="ans" data-new="1"><p>The other side says what the figure should be, and you are asked to confirm it. If you still disagree, the record reads Contested and keeps both versions. Nobody can remove either one.</p></div></details><details class="qa"><summary><span>What happens when I decline a record?</span><svg class="chev" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-cd"/></svg></summary><div class="ans" data-new="1"><p>The person who wrote it sees that you declined it. It stays off your books and can't be sealed.</p></div></details><details class="qa"><summary><span>What does Contested mean?</span><svg class="chev" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-cd"/></svg></summary><div class="ans" data-new="1"><p>You and the other side don't agree on the record. Both versions are kept, and neither can be removed. Sawaza is a witness, not a judge.</p></div></details><details class="qa"><summary><span>What does "Sawa. Sealed." mean?</span><svg class="chev" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-cd"/></svg></summary><div class="ans" data-new="1"><p>Everyone named on the record has signed it. You both hold the same copy, and any change shows.</p></div></details><details class="qa"><summary><span>Can a signed record be changed?</span><svg class="chev" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-cd"/></svg></summary><div class="ans" data-new="1"><p>A signed record is sealed, so any change shows. A disagreement keeps both versions, and a correction is a new record both sides sign.</p></div></details><details class="qa"><summary><span>Is a record's history kept?</span><svg class="chev" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-cd"/></svg></summary><div class="ans" data-new="1"><p>Yes. A record's page shows who wrote it, who confirmed it, on which phone and when. A signed record is sealed, so any change shows, and a disagreement keeps both versions.</p></div></details></section>
<section class="topic" id="groups" aria-labelledby="groups-h"><h2 id="groups-h">Groups</h2><details class="qa"><summary><span>What kinds of groups can I start?</span><svg class="chev" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-cd"/></svg></summary><div class="ans" data-new="1"><p>Savings &amp; Investment (a SACCO or chama), Cash round, Household and Other, for a club, a committee or a burial society.</p></div></details><details class="qa"><summary><span>Who does what in a group?</span><svg class="chev" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-cd"/></svg></summary><div class="ans" data-new="1"><p>Officers act for the group from the avatar menu and record its money. Records made while acting as the group are the group's, and its people confirm their own lines. An admin's powers come only from acting as the group: on their own account, they are a member like everyone else. In the beta, each group or business account has one admin, who signs for the group on each of its records. Its people are members, admins and the owner. Titles such as Chair, Treasurer and Secretary are the group's own words.</p></div></details><details class="qa"><summary><span>How do I add members?</span><svg class="chev" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-cd"/></svg></summary><div class="ans" data-new="1"><p>Type a number and Sawaza checks whether they are on Sawaza, invite someone already on it, or add a name only. A name only is kept by the group, and only the group sees it.</p></div></details><details class="qa"><summary><span>How does a cash round work on Sawaza?</span><svg class="chev" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-cd"/></svg></summary><div class="ans" data-new="1"><p>Everyone pays the same amount each cycle, and one member takes the pot each turn. Sawaza keeps who has paid, the payout order and the reminders. A button records a payment; it never pays.</p></div></details><details class="qa"><summary><span>What do savings group members see?</span><svg class="chev" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-cd"/></svg></summary><div class="ans" data-new="1"><p>A register for the group and a passbook for each member. The register is added up from the group's own records, so nothing is typed in twice. A passbook shows each member's savings and shares, and members see their own on the group's contact page. A member who leaves keeps their line in the register.</p></div></details><details class="qa"><summary><span>How do I start a group?</span><svg class="chev" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-cd"/></svg></summary><div class="ans" data-new="1"><p>Start it from your own account. Choose Group, then the kind nearest yours. Add members by phone number, by name only, or someone already on Sawaza.</p></div></details><details class="qa"><summary><span>Can a group lend to its members?</span><svg class="chev" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-cd"/></svg></summary><div class="ans" data-new="1"><p>Yes. Loans to members carry a schedule: the day of each payment, what was paid back and what is still owed. In the beta, a group's loans are an open book: its members can read them.</p></div></details><details class="qa"><summary><span>How does a household work?</span><svg class="chev" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-cd"/></svg></summary><div class="ans" data-new="1"><p>A home's money kept by two partners. Your spouse is invited as an owner, and you stand on the same side of every record. The bills you share and the things you own together are in one place both of you can read.</p></div></details></section>
<section class="topic" id="business" aria-labelledby="business-h"><h2 id="business-h">Businesses</h2><details class="qa"><summary><span>What kinds of business can use Sawaza?</span><svg class="chev" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-cd"/></svg></summary><div class="ans" data-new="1"><p>A sole business, a company, a partnership or a cooperative, each with an account of its own, kept apart from your own money.</p></div></details><details class="qa"><summary><span>Is the business's money kept apart from mine?</span><svg class="chev" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-cd"/></svg></summary><div class="ans" data-new="1"><p>Yes. The business keeps its own account and its own books. Your personal records stay in yours.</p></div></details><details class="qa"><summary><span>How do invoices work?</span><svg class="chev" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-cd"/></svg></summary><div class="ans" data-new="1"><p>One credit sale, one record. The seller holds the invoice and the buyer holds the bill, and both sign it.</p></div></details><details class="qa"><summary><span>Can I lend with a payment plan?</span><svg class="chev" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-cd"/></svg></summary><div class="ans" data-new="1"><p>Yes. A loan has terms: a type, a rate, a number of payments and any fees. Sawaza works out the schedule and what is still owed. The borrower accepts the terms on their own phone before the loan stands. Each payment has a day, the part that is the loan, the part that is interest, and a status. A payment you record is split between late fee, fees, interest and the loan.</p></div></details><details class="qa"><summary><span>Who can act for my business?</span><svg class="chev" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-cd"/></svg></summary><div class="ans" data-new="1"><p>Officers act for the business and sign for it. Records made while acting for it are the business's, never the officer's own. A viewer only reads the books. In the beta, each group or business account has one admin. Titles are the business's own words: Manager, Director, Administrator, or one you type.</p></div></details><details class="qa"><summary><span>Can I sell on credit with a deposit?</span><svg class="chev" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-cd"/></svg></summary><div class="ans" data-new="1"><p>Yes. A sale on credit can carry a deposit paid now, with the rest due on the day you set. Your customer confirms what they owe and by when, on their own phone. Each part payment is recorded against it, and the figure left goes down on both sides.</p></div></details><details class="qa"><summary><span>What does a customer's account show?</span><svg class="chev" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-cd"/></svg></summary><div class="ans" data-new="1"><p>Each customer's invoices, part payments and what is left, signed by them. Each person shows one net figure: what they owe you, or what you owe them. Cleared is shown when the debt is paid off.</p></div></details><details class="qa"><summary><span>Do I have to switch on books?</span><svg class="chev" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-cd"/></svg></summary><div class="ans" data-new="1"><p>No. A business keeps its books from its first record. They show money in and out each month, across every space you keep.</p></div></details><details class="qa"><summary><span>Does Sawaza do quotations and receipts?</span><svg class="chev" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-cd"/></svg></summary><div class="ans" data-new="1"><p>Not in the beta. Quotations and receipts, line items and templates, and statements for your customers are not there yet.</p></div></details></section>
  </div>
  <div class="none" id="faq-none" hidden data-new="1">
    <p><b>No answer matches that yet.</b></p>
    <p>Try another word, or email us at hello@sawaza.app and we will answer there.</p>
  </div>
</div></section>
<section class="sec" id="contact"><div class="wrap">
  <div class="sec-head"><p class="q">Still stuck?</p><h2 class="h2">Talk to us.</h2><p class="lede" data-new="1">Email us, and we will answer there.</p></div>
  <div class="ways">
    <div class="way"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="3" y="5" width="18" height="14" rx="2"/><path d="m4 7 8 6 8-6"/></svg><b>Email</b><p>hello@sawaza.app</p></div>
  </div>
  <div class="next-row"><a class="tlink" href="/how-it-works">See how it works <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><a class="tlink" href="/trust">Trust and privacy <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div>
</div></section>
<script>
(function(){
  var input=document.getElementById('faq-q');if(!input)return;
  var items=[].slice.call(document.querySelectorAll('#page-help .qa'));
  var topics=[].slice.call(document.querySelectorAll('#page-help .topic'));
  var none=document.getElementById('faq-none'),count=document.getElementById('faq-count');
  items.forEach(function(d){d._t=d.textContent.toLowerCase();d._open=d.open});
  function run(){
    var q=input.value.trim().toLowerCase(),words=q.split(/\s+/).filter(Boolean),shown=0;
    items.forEach(function(d){
      var hit=words.every(function(w){return d._t.indexOf(w)>-1});
      d.hidden=!hit;if(hit)shown++;
      d.open=words.length?hit:d._open;
    });
    topics.forEach(function(s){s.hidden=!s.querySelector('.qa:not([hidden])')});
    none.hidden=shown>0;
    count.textContent=words.length?(shown===1?'1 answer':shown+' answers'):'';
  }
  input.addEventListener('input',run);
  var p=new URLSearchParams(location.search).get('q');if(p){input.value=p;run()}
})();
</script>
</Base>
